It's often done that commands typed on the command line are put into
scripts and use the scripts as simple commands (not for one-shot ones
but often it turns out that you need those commands often and have an
advantage doing so), and these scripts are occasionally extended later
and grow. Keep in mind that csh is inappropriate for shell programming,
don't use it! (For details see Tom Christiansen's historic article:
"Csh Programming Considered Harmful".)

